/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md:78:## agent-browser Usage
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md:80:Vercel's agent-browser is the single tool for browser automation, QA verification, and any browser navigation. It is a native CLI driving Chrome/Chromium over CDP and manages its own browser, so no manual Chrome launch or sandbox flags are needed.
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md:84:- Install once: `npm i -g agent-browser && agent-browser install`.
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md:85:- Load the version-matched guide before using it: `agent-browser skills get core` (overview + common patterns) or `agent-browser skills get core --full` (full command reference). For exploratory testing and bug hunts load `agent-browser skills get dogfood`; run `agent-browser skills list` for the rest.
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md:90:agent-browser open https://mirror-help.arrayhash.com/wp-admin   # navigate
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md:91:agent-browser snapshot -i                                       # interactive elements + @eN refs
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md:92:agent-browser click @e3                                         # act on a ref
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md:93:agent-browser snapshot -i                                       # re-snapshot after any change
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md:94:agent-browser screenshot --full /tmp/state.png                 # capture to judge the UI
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md:100:- Use isolated sessions for different auth contexts: `agent-browser --session admin …`, `--session customer …`, `--session guest …`. Persist or restore login with `--session-name`, `state save`/`state load`, or the auth vault as needed.
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md:101:- Prefer precise waits over fixed sleeps: `wait @ref`, `wait --text "…"`, `wait --url "**/wp-admin"`, `wait --load networkidle`.
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md:103:- Close sessions when done: `agent-browser close --all`.
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md:145:- asset handles, admin routes, and runtime data objects
/home/server-manager/www/arrayhash/mirror-help.arrayhash.com/public/wp-content/plugins/AGENTS.md:187:Native browser dialogs (`window.alert`, `window.confirm`, `window.prompt`) are **forbidden** anywhere in this codebase. Every action button that triggers an AJAX/REST call MUST also surface a visible loading state. Use the project's shared helpers — never roll your own.
